course: dictionary
lesson: 9296
title: One word, many meanings: spear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Spear» can name a thing, or it can name an action. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, and ask: is this a thing or something someone does?
explain: «There they find Taffy making daisy-chains and Tegumai happily spearing small carp with his mended spear.» The word «spearing» is something Tegumai does, so it is an action. The word «spear» at the end is a thing he holds, a long pointed weapon. The clues are «happily spearing» and «his mended spear».
explain: Taffy says, «There wasn't lots of spears.» Lots of comes before a thing you can count, so spears is a noun, a name for things. Now test your meaning: put «weapons» in the place of «spears» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A spear is a long weapon or tool with a pointed tip, used for throwing or stabbing.
fact: «Spear» can also mean a long, thin, pointed shoot of a plant, such as «a spear of asparagus».
fact: To spear means to push something pointed into something, such as «spearing food with a fork», or to catch or hunt with a spear.
fact: In history lessons, early humans and many peoples hunted and fished with spears.
fact: «In 1822 a stork in Germany was found with an African spear in its neck; it helped prove storks spend winter in Africa.»
exercise: In «Tegumai happily spearing small carp with his mended spear», what does spearing mean? | Drawing pictures of fish | Cutting the carp into small pieces | Swimming fast through the river | *Catching fish with a pointed weapon
exercise: «Asparagus comes in spears.» In this sentence, what is a spear? | A tool for picking up food | A weapon for hunting | A small fish | *A long, thin, pointed shoot of a plant
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a long pointed weapon. | lessons | history | humans | *spear
test: In «to spear a chip with your fork», what does spear mean? | To cut a chip into thin strips | *To stab food with a pointed fork to pick it up | To cook a chip in hot oil | To throw a chip across the room
test: In the phrase «spear fishing», what does spear mean? | Cooking fish in a pan | Swimming with fish in a river | *Catching fish with a spear | Drawing fish on paper
exam: Taffy says «There wasn't lots of spears.» Why must spears be a noun here? | Because spears always means an action | Because Taffy is talking about a fork | Because it ends with s, so it must be a verb | *Because lots of is followed by a thing you can count
